// @hash 11df3c8abebc
// @legend — how to write this file (rewritten by ./singularity build; edits inside this block are lost):
//   Item: "<key>" (terse; <key> is "<pluginId>:<id>")
//   Hide: { "item": "<key>", "hidden": true }
//   Spacer (gap): { "type": "spacer", "id": "<unique-id>" } — grows to push every item after it to the far end of the row (title left, chips right); at most one per slot. Use it instead of a second slot.
//   Divider (rule): { "type": "divider", "id": "<unique-id>" } — a hairline rule between the items either side of it, turned to the slot's flow (flat in a column such as a sidebar's footer rows, upright in a row such as a toolbar).
//   Group: { "type": "header", "label": "<title>", "collapsed": false, "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
//   Overflow (⋯ menu): { "type": "overflow", "id": "<unique-id>", "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
// A horizontal pane header, read left to right: what the canvas is OF on the
// left, what you can do to the canvas on the right.
//
// The pane's own title first, then three small icons that are facts about the
// prototype itself — `copy-id` (copy its id for a prompt or a CLI command),
// `pin` (pin it to the gallery's Pinned section) and `done` (the Done checkbox),
// the last two the same shared flags as the gallery card's. All keep one size
// in every state, so a click never moves the header.
//
// After the spacer, the canvas's own actions, which take no vertical room from
// the canvas by living here: `layout` (`Side by side | Swipe`, shown only with
// exactly two frames) and `add` (`+ Frame`, then one `+ <source>` per frame
// source — `+ Real app`), and last `open-canvas` (the canvas as it is, in a
// chromeless new browser tab, for the whole screen to compare in).
{
  "items": [
    "primitives.pane:title",
    "apps.prototypes.copy-id:copy-id",
    "apps.prototypes.gallery:pin",
    "apps.prototypes.gallery:done",
    { "type": "spacer", "id": "spacer-1" },
    "apps.prototypes.canvas:layout",
    "apps.prototypes.canvas:add",
    "apps.prototypes.present:open-canvas"
  ]
}
